<div class="mw-parser-output"><h1>Throw</h1>
<p>Skill
Class: Ranger (guild level 20)
</p><p>Usage:
</p>
<pre>throw &lt;weapon&gt; at &lt;someone&gt;
</pre>
<p>Example:
</p>
<pre>throw dagger at orc
</pre>
<p>Hurls a weapon you carry, or the one in your hand, at someone in the 
room: even someone you can't reach because you are fighting another. It 
hits like a blow from that weapon, and then it lies on the ground (or in 
your victim), so go and pick it up.
</p><p>Your throw skill, with your dexterity and strength, against your target's 
dexterity, decides whether you hit. A heavier weapon costs more endurance 
to throw, and a two-handed one needs both hands free. Only weapons can be 
thrown, and not bows, crossbows or slings: use those to shoot (see 
<a cmd='#'>Help Shoot</a>). To throw at a player, both of you must have signed the Book 
of Blood. You must be standing.
</p><p><br />
See Also:
</p>
<pre>&gt; <a cmd='#'>Help Shoot</a>
&gt; <a cmd='#'>Help Weapons</a>
&gt; <a cmd='#'>Help Ranger Skills</a>
</pre>




</div>